{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 12 that avoid forbidden substrings \"111\" and \"000\". So no three consecutive same bits. Count sequences of length n with no run of 3 same bits. This is classic recurrence. Let a_n be number of sequences length n ending with run of length 1 of some bit, b_n ending with run length 2. Actually we can use DP with states: last two bits? Let's do recurrence: Let A_n be number of sequences length n ending with a single bit (i.e., last two bits different). Let B_n be number ending with two identical bits (run length 2). For n=1: A_1=2 (0 or1), B_1=0. For n=2: sequences length2: \"00\",\"01\",\"10\",\"11\". Those ending with run length1: \"01\",\"10\" => A_2=2. Ending with run length2: \"00\",\"11\" => B_2=2. For n>2: To get A_n: last two bits differ, so last bit different from previous. So we can append a bit different from previous bit. If previous state was A_{n-1} (run length1), previous last bit is some bit, we can append opposite bit => run length1. If previous state was B_{n-1} (run length2), previous last two bits same, last bit is that bit, we can append opposite bit => run length1. So A_n = A_{n-1} + B_{n-1}. For B_n: last two bits same, so last bit same as previous. To get run length2, previous state must be A_{n-1} (run length1) and we append same bit. Cannot come from B_{n-1} because that would create run length3. So B_n = A_{n-1}. So recurrence: A_n = A_{n-1}+B_{n-1} = A_{n-1}+A_{n-2}. B_n = A_{n-1}. So we can compute up to n=12. Let's compute:\n\nn=1: A1=2, B1=0\nn=2: A2=2, B2=2\nn=3: A3 = A2+B2 =2+2=4; B3 = A2=2\nn=4: A4 = A3+B3 =4+2=6; B4 = A3=4\nn=5: A5 = A4+B4 =6+4=10; B5 = A4=6\nn=6: A6 = A5+B5 =10+6=16; B6 = A5=10\nn=7: A7 = A6+B6 =16+10=26; B7 = A6=16\nn=8: A8 = A7+B7 =26+16=42; B8 = A7=26\nn=9: A9 = A8+B8 =42+26=68; B9 = A8=42\nn=10: A10 = A9+B9 =68+42=110; B10 = A9=68\nn=11: A11 = A10+B10 =110+68=178; B11 = A10=110\nn=12: A12 = A11+B11 =178+110=288; B12 = A11=178\n\nTotal sequences length12 = A12+B12 = 288+178=466.\n\nThus answer 466."}}],"created":1790980423,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":4111,"total_tokens":4879,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-IYsllhsuolkuu1YmtE5bEo1CD3z8ZoS3","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4111,"prompt_ms":498.703,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.12130941376793966,"prompt_per_second":8243.383336374556,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2386.345,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.111271186440678,"predicted_per_second":321.4120338844551}}